    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="1061" n="967" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg967"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Lothrop.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department in State.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 24,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 93.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 119 of the 1st
                    instant, in which you send a paragraph and translation from the Journal de St.
                    Petersbourg relative to the proposed new Russian law of naturalization which
                    will permit Russian subjects to obtain naturalization abroad. This is an
                    encouraging sign.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
